      "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\n  The Rust frontend decodes each logprobs candidate independently with\r\n  decode(&[token_id], skip_special_tokens). The general tiktoken decode path\r\n  allocates temporary token ID and byte buffers for every call, even though the\r\n  decoded text for each known token ID is already stored in TokenMetadata.\r\n\r\n  Use the precomputed token text when exactly one known token ID is decoded.\r\n  Special tokens still honor skip_special_tokens, unknown IDs fall back to the\r\n  existing backend behavior, and empty or multi-token inputs remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n  This removes repeated allocation and backend decoding work from the logprobs\r\n  hot path. The targeted single-token decode benchmark showed:\r\n```\r\n   Backend           Before        After    Time reduction\r\n  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\r\n   riptoken       720.67 ns    243.63 ns             66.2%\r\n  ─────────────  ───────────  ───────────  ────────────────\r\n   tiktoken-rs    1.1643 µs    235.98 ns             79.7%\r\n```\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```\r\n  cargo nextest run -p vllm-tokenizer  tiktoken --no-fail-fast\r\n  cargo nextest run -p vllm-tokenizer --all-features --locked --no-fail-fast\r\n  cargo bench -p vllm-tokenizer  --bench tiktoken  --  tiktoken_decode_single_tokens\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
